# Shell scripts must stay LF. A CRLF line ending on the shebang line makes the
# Linux kernel look for an interpreter named "/bin/sh\r", which fails with a
# bare "no such file or directory" that names a file which plainly exists —
# one of the harder Docker-on-Windows errors to diagnose. This repo is edited
# from Windows, so pin it rather than rely on each clone's core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else consumed by Linux tooling.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
